# ==============================================================================
# AI-Shark Environment Configuration - Root Directory
# ==============================================================================
# NOTE: This is a reference file. For actual configuration:
#
# Backend Configuration:  backend/.env.example -> backend/.env
# Frontend Configuration: frontend/.env.example -> frontend/.env
#
# ==============================================================================

# BACKEND SETUP (backend/.env)
# =============================
# The backend configuration includes:
#
# - Multi-LLM Configuration
#   * Vision tasks (Phase 1): Google Gemini or Groq Llama 4
#   * Text tasks (Phases 2-5): Groq Llama 4 Scout
#   * Fallback: Groq Llama 4 Maverick
#
# - API Keys
#   * GROQ_API_KEY (required for text tasks)
#   * GOOGLE_API_KEY (required if using Gemini for vision)
#
# - Storage Configuration
#   * USE_GCS=false (local development)
#   * USE_GCS=true (production with Google Cloud Storage)
#   * GCS_BUCKET_NAME=ai-shark-outputs
#
# - API Configuration
#   * API_HOST=0.0.0.0
#   * API_PORT=8000
#   * MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB=100
#
# - Mock Mode (testing without API calls)
#   * USE_MOCK_LLM=false
#
# Full configuration available at: backend/.env.example

# FRONTEND SETUP (frontend/.env)
# ===============================
# The frontend configuration includes:
#
# - Development:
#   * VITE_API_URL=/api (uses Vite proxy)
#
# - Production:
#   * VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend-url.run.app/api
#
# Full configuration available at: frontend/.env.example

# QUICK START
# ===========
# 1. Copy backend environment:
#    cd backend && cp .env.example .env
#
# 2. Copy frontend environment:
#    cd frontend && cp .env.example .env
#
# 3. Edit backend/.env with your API keys:
#    - Add your GROQ_API_KEY
#    - Add your GOOGLE_API_KEY (if using Gemini)
#
# 4. Start development:
#    docker-compose up
#
# 5. Access the application:
#    - Frontend: http://localhost:3000
#    - Backend: http://localhost:8000
#    - API Docs: http://localhost:8000/docs

# DEPLOYMENT
# ==========
# For detailed deployment instructions, see DEPLOYMENT.md
#
# - Backend: Deploy to Google Cloud Run
# - Frontend: Deploy to Vercel
# - Complete setup guide with environment variables
